.TH QUANUX-TRANSLATOR 7 "FEBRUARY 2026" "QuanuX Biological Sovereignty" "QuanuX System Manual"
.SH NAME
quanux-translator \- The Universal Translator (OnixS SDK Integration)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B make -f Makefile.onixs
.SH DESCRIPTION
The QuanuX Cell operates a \fB16-cycle\fR DMA perception rate (The Neural Singularity). However, pure speed is useless if the Nucleus does not comprehend the binary dialect of the external matching engine.

To achieve \fBLinguistic Singularity\fR, the QuanuX outer membrane employs the \fBUniversal Translator\fR. 

By default, the cell compiles with a "Sanctified Stub"—an altruistic interface ensuring the core execution loop remains intact and operational for simulation. To communicate with the native execution wires of the exchange (SBE, Native Binary, etc.), the cell must undergo an \fBInjectable Sovereignty\fR graft.
.SH INJECTABLE SOVEREIGNTY (The Chassis and The Engine)
QuanuX acts as the 16-cycle \fBChassis\fR. The OnixS Solarflare Handler acts as the proprietary \fBEngine\fR.

When authorized users possess the permissioned \fBOnixS SDK\fR and API key, they may fuse the two halves during the ritual of compilation.
.SH THE RITUAL OF COMPILATION
The QuanuX kernel detects the SDK via the pre-processor directive \fB#ifdef HAS_ONIXS\fR.

When triggered, the Stub is replaced by the \fBOnixS_Proprietary_Graft\fR. This grafts the true Binary Order Handler directly into the Synaptic Bridge (`quanux_shm(4)`).
.SH THE WARNING
The true binary dialects of the matching engines are protected frequencies. Attempts to execute live orders on direct native feeds without the proprietary SDK will result in instant rejection by the market gateway. The Universal Translator requires the Key.
